;;; Register: what counts as formal written English for emdysi.
;;;
;;; The ERG marks contracted auxiliaries (|we'll|, |it's|, |they're|) as
;;; GENRE nonformal, so that a sentence with one has no strict analysis.
;;; Its own comment (auxverbs/lextypes, contracted_aux_word, DPF 2015) says
;;; why: to keep the generator from producing |*Here, Kim's|, "as long as
;;; we use root_strict for generation". emdysi parses edited prose, where
;;; contractions are standard (the Rust book, the Kubernetes docs), so this
;;; redefinition drops the GENRE constraint; everything else is the ERG's.
;;; (A later TDL definition of a type replaces the earlier one, as in ACE.)

:begin :type.

contracted_aux_word := word &
  [ INFLECTD na,
    ALTS [ VPELLIP -,
           SQPNCT - ],
    SYNSEM.LOCAL.CAT [ HEAD.CNTRCTD +,
		       VAL.COMPS.FIRST expressed_synsem ] ].

:end :type.
